Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MEASUREMENT ONLY: decouple the get-side kick from the wait
 knob

Throwaway variant for the decomposition matrix. On current main-line
behavior the demand-side kick fires only when ssd_get_wait_ms > 0, so a
zero/nonzero wait comparison cannot isolate the wait's benefit. This
variant fires the kick whenever prefetch is enabled, letting arm 3
(kick on, wait off) be measured. Do NOT merge this anywhere.
---
 mooncake-store/src/real_client.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mooncake-store/src/real_client.cpp b/mooncake-store/src/real_client.cpp
--- a/mooncake-store/src/real_client.cpp
+++ b/mooncake-store/src/real_client.cpp
@@ -7867,7 +7867,10 @@ RealClient::batch_get_into_multi_buffers_internal(
                 now_ms, ssd_get_wait_ms_, lease_floor_ms);
         }
     }
-    if (get_wait) {
+    // MEASUREMENT-ONLY VARIANT (kick_decouple.patch): fire the kick whenever
+    // prefetch is on, not only when the wait is enabled, so the matrix can
+    // isolate the wait's benefit from the kick's. Not for the PR.
+    if (enable_ssd_prefetch_ && prefetcher_) {
         // Demand-side kick: a batch headed for SSD gets one promotion
         // attempt for its disk keys. ignore_cooldown bypasses only the
         // client-side throttle's backoff, never a master-side gate (the
--
